* OPA365 macromodel written for this project (not the vendor model).
*
* Datasheet numbers it uses (TI OPA365, 5 V supply, typical):
*   gain bandwidth product 50 MHz
*   slew rate 25 V/us
*   open loop gain 120 dB
*   quiescent current 4.6 mA
*   output swing to within about 10 mV of either rail at light load
*   short circuit current 65 mA, used as the output current limit
* Assumed (not table values):
*   open loop output resistance 40 ohm,
*   second pole at 90 MHz (gives about 60 degrees of unity gain margin).
* Not modelled: noise, CMRR, PSRR, input capacitance, input bias current,
* the input crossover region (the real part has none), temperature drift.
*
* Pins: non-inverting input, inverting input, positive supply, negative supply, output
.subckt OPA365 inp inn vcc vee out params: vos=0 ro=40 isc=65m
.param gbw=50e6 sr=25e6 aol=1e6 c1v=10p
.param imax={sr*c1v} gm1={2*3.14159265359*gbw*c1v} r1v={aol/gm1}
.param vsw=0.010 cp2={1/(2*3.14159265359*90e6*1e3)}
* supply current
Iq vcc vee DC 4.6m
* mid supply reference for the gain node
Bmid mid 0 V = 0.5*(V(vcc)+V(vee))
* offset voltage source on the non-inverting input
Vos inp inp_i DC {vos}
* stage 1: slew limited transconductance into an RC (dominant pole 50 Hz)
B1 mid n1 I = {imax}*tanh((V(inp_i)-V(inn))*{gm1}/{imax})
R1 n1 mid {r1v}
C1 n1 mid {c1v}
* soft clamp of the gain node 10 mV inside the rails (prevents wind-up).
* Clamp conductance 1 S with a 2 mV knee; the guard avoids exp() overflow.
Bclp n1 0 I = ((V(n1)-V(vcc)+{vsw}) > 0.06 ? (V(n1)-V(vcc)+{vsw}) : 0.002*ln(1+exp((V(n1)-V(vcc)+{vsw})/0.002))) - ((V(vee)+{vsw}-V(n1)) > 0.06 ? (V(vee)+{vsw}-V(n1)) : 0.002*ln(1+exp((V(vee)+{vsw}-V(n1))/0.002)))
* stage 2: non-dominant pole at 90 MHz
B2 n2a 0 V = V(n1)
R2 n2a n2 1k
C2 n2 0 {cp2}
* output stage: Thevenin source with resistance ro and current limit isc
Bo 0 out I = {isc}*tanh((V(n2)-V(out))/({ro}*{isc}))
* the output current is drawn from the positive supply when sourcing; the
* split is a smooth max(I, 0) with a 1 uA knee so the solver sees no kink
Bsup vcc 0 I = 0.5*({isc}*tanh((V(n2)-V(out))/({ro}*{isc})) + sqrt({isc}*tanh((V(n2)-V(out))/({ro}*{isc}))*{isc}*tanh((V(n2)-V(out))/({ro}*{isc})) + 1e-12))
.ends OPA365
